        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sometimes, we use food emojis when "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "texting",
            "ref": "v-text"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But have you ever asked yourself, “What would they look (and taste) like in real life?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Meet 20-year-old Ash Baber from England. He is making food emojis into real things. It all started with the birthday cake emoji. He thought it looked "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "strange",
            "ref": "v-strange"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". On top of the cake, there were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "regular",
            "ref": "v-regular"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " candles—the ones you put on a table."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Baber then made this cake in real life. His cake looked "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "exactly",
            "zh": "完全"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " like the emoji, and he didn’t use birthday cake candles, of course! People loved Baber’s cake. They asked him to make the cupcake too. So he did. Then came the bubble tea, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "doughnut",
            "zh": "甜甜圈"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "..."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i2",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img2"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Baber’s foods look fun. He "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pays attention to",
            "zh": "在意"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " every "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "detail",
            "ref": "v-detail"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". To make the cupcake, he stood in his kitchen for a long time. He put "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sprinkles",
            "zh": "糖屑"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on one by one!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Want to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "have a go",
            "ref": "v-have-a-go"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Well, study the emoji carefully. “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Zoom in",
            "zh": "放大"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as much as you can”, said Baber."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
